        "subject": "LU-21236 ptlrpc: free culled request buffers outside scp_lock",
        "message": "LU-21236 ptlrpc: free culled request buffers outside scp_lock\n\nSince LU-18687, OBD_FREE_LARGE() frees vmalloc memory with\nvfree(), which can sleep. ptlrpc_server_drop_request() frees\nculled request buffers this way while holding scp_lock. On a\nkernel without CONFIG_PREEMPT_COUNT, such as RHEL 8, the\nholder can be scheduled out while the other service threads\non its CPT spin on the lock, and the server soft locks up.\n\nCollect the buffers to free under the lock and free them\nafter dropping it.\n\nFixes: 94b21a46bfa1 (\"LU-18687 obd: don't always use vfree_atomic\")\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Idf131b5be460adb3d91e4a1db447e7b347b52ba8\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master",
